<p>T.L. at your service!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Here&nbsp;lies&nbsp;crit&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Bye&nbsp;bye&nbsp;crit&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Just to give you a heads up, tropes like &quot;don't contain this anomaly or something bad will happen&quot; is a pretty major cliche in the SCP universe. However, I do see some potential in this. When you say contain, do you mean that the person has to feel lol they are contained/imprisoned on order for the effects to take place? I mean, being in anything like a house could be considered contained. Your concept doesn't seem to suggest that it's literal though. Also, I'm assuming that the blood humanoid can escape more easily from imprisonment than the human, due to fluidity. But after all the other people are killed, would't the human still be imprisoned? Your concept didn't mention about the blood figure helping the person escape.</p>
<p>Moving on, I find the idea of the Foundation finding ways to contain something like this is quite interesting. I'm just worried about the execution. I like that you're going for something like &quot;fool the person into thinking they are not contained when they really are&quot;. I'd like to know how exactly the Foundation plans to stop this criminal from committing crime while working under them. Other than that, any possible chance you could show the whole sequence of events from how they got caught from the Foundation to how they became a janitor that keeps commiting crime under them? I also think if you tried nudging an interview in there, it could be beneficial for your audience to get to learn more about this criminal personality and characteristics.</p>
<p>Overall, try working out a sequence of events for the narrative to better help others have a better picture. Also work out on the other points I mentioned to clear up some plot holes.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
If you have any questions regarding my critique, please let me know. You are welcome to PM me for another look, or you may follow up with someone from the Butterfly Squad Roster or IRC Chat rooms.
