<p>Thanks again for the crit dude,</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Now&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;stuffs</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">:)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It seems there may be some miscommunication going around here, so let me try to clear this up first.</p>
<p>The foundation's method of containment is to hire them as a full time janitor for one of their front companies. This serves to help keep an eye on them for the majority of the day. For the rest, I was thinking maybe install/hack cameras near frequent visiting spot, (Apartment, Store, Etc) and install a gps chip in their sleep for the rest. As for the crime, they are doing this while employed as a janitor. After 1-2 of these attempts (both failed), the manager of the front will speak to them, threaten job security and say &quot;With a rap sheet that long, your lucky to be working HERE.&quot; This will dissuade them from future crimes. The only time I will have them breach containment is at the initial retrieval, where they have little to no information on him.</p>
<p>As for the narrative, I can remove the focus of it from the blood creature. Along with his past with the GoI, I'm going for a bit of a redemption arc with him eventually becoming a senior janitor.</p>
<p>Relating to the senior janitor, I'm considering him to have increased red and white blood cell counts, allowing him to keep working at the foundation at present day (about 95-110 Years old). I think it would help sell the final &quot;I was a bad guy, but now I'm working hard to pay my debt to society.&quot; arc. Or I could not do that, still iffy on it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
I want YOU! To have a nice day :D
