<p>Apologies for the delay, life's taken a bit of a turn.</p>
<p>I can kinda get on board with what's here, so my main concern is just making this character someone the audience can root for. Starting them out as, from a literary perspective, evil, and then transitioning them into the protagonist, takes a lot of work. In your own words can you describe why the audience is going to like this character and root for them?</p>
