<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>In an old audio log found by the foundation, during questioning for why he wants to join the spirit, they ask him why he wants to join them.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hmm, here's a word of advice about audio logs like this: You're gonna want to use them to really emphasize this character's personality and vernacular by contrast. Ideally, since he's a bad guy at this point in the narrative, he should be fairly abrasive to Foundation personnel but you're gonna have to juggle that with seeing him be endearing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I could have a video feed cut out, but the audio would still be there, this would be where I would put the audio log, which by what your saying, I assume is actually recorded by me.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This log things sounds good, but there's no need to record audio like that, you can just write it out.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>As for highlighting the attempts, which I assume you mean are the crimes, I could have a log of all the actions he does like this</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I struggle a bit with crit like this, since I don't want to infringe upon authorial intent, but I was thinking more along the lines of an addendum with a brief description of what he did, followed by a panicked phone call between him and the Foundation as he's locking himself in the back of the store after being overwhelmed by the police presence.</p>
<p>The reason I recommend this approach is because it's just a better setting for character growth and revelation —&nbsp;you've got two parties in a high-stakes environment, one of which is attempting to swallow his pride enough to ask the other for help. The stakes and the interaction tend to produce more dynamic characters than a simple timeline.</p>
<hr />
<p>So I think I'm getting a better understanding of how this is shaping up, and I think this is gonna be the most solid narrative we've devised so far.</p>
<ol>
<li>Dude joins the Spirit, makes some connections, eventually falls into the Foundation's pocket after their disbandment due to him being incompetent without backup.</li>
<li>He has an intake interview where his character is established to the reader and some of his backstory is illuminated.</li>
<li>In an effort to mitigate future containment breaches, the Foundation positions him in a heavily-monitored janitorial position with some promise of upward mobility.</li>
<li>A combination of pride and an itch in his gut leads him to breach containment, attempting to pull off a crime to prove he's really a criminal after all; this goes south and he requests re-containment by the Foundation.</li>
<li>Following re-containment he is approached by one of his old contacts in the Spectre who offers him a way back to his old life; he comes close to taking the deal but some unspecified thing that's occurred in the narrative previously compels him to reject the offer — maybe he realizes that his past wasn't anything he should be chasing after.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-976918-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-976918-1')">1</a></sup></li>
<li>He eventually works his way back up to a senior position on the janitorial staff.</li>
</ol>
<p>Does that generally sound like a story you want to go after?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-976918-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-976918-1')">1</a>. I'm specifically imagining a part of the phone conversation where the Foundation asks if he used his anomalous ability to hurt anyone and he says he doesn't do that anymore and seems horrified.</div>
</div>

